You can generate a new X.509 certificate and key with the following bash command:
openssl req -new -x509 -days 3652 -nodes -out sp.cert -keyout sp.key

Your new certification will be stored as "sp.cert" in the same directory that
you execute the openssl command in. The associated key will be stored in
the same place and will be named "sp.key". yvideo-py will look for sp.cert
and sp.key in the yvideo/saml_config/certs directory
